      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Urapidil, a lipophilic basic amine with aromatic groups, had an absolute oral bioavailability of 78% (72-84%) in healthy male volunteers, supporting high F for the similarly lipophilic basic query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C25"],
      "claim": "Donepezil, a lipophilic basic CNS drug containing an indanone and benzylpiperidine, has an oral bioavailability of 100% in humans, supporting high F for the query's indane/amine scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C20"],
      "claim": "Diphenhydramine, a lipophilic tertiary-amine antihistamine, had an absolute oral bioavailability of 42±5% in elderly subjects, with other studies reporting 35-72%, all above the 20% threshold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C31"],
      "claim": "Imipramine-N-oxide, a tricyclic propylamine with an N-aryl motif, showed approximately 100% systemic availability after oral dosing in healthy volunteers, supporting high F for the query's propylamine/N-aryl structure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C36"],
      "claim": "Oxcarbazepine, an N-aryl heterocyclic drug, had 89% absolute bioavailability of its active moiety in healthy adults, supporting high F for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C22"],
      "claim": "Laquinimod, a lipophilic N-phenyl carboxamide, has approximately 80-90% oral bioavailability in humans, supporting high F for the query's N-phenyl and lipophilic features.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved experimental analogues with high transfer scores report absolute oral bioavailability values above the 20% threshold, mostly in the 55-100% range. The query's lipophilic basic amine/indane structure is consistent with good absorption and high oral bioavailability, so the prediction is high.",
